<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RiderIlSpy user-facing strings (C# / ReSharper side).
  Locale overlays live in Strings.<lang>.resx (none yet — translatable infra only).
  Looked up at runtime via RiderIlSpy.Resources.Strings — see Strings.cs.

  Banner comment prefixes (e.g. "// Decompiled with RiderIlSpy", "// Type: ")
  intentionally stay in English. Those lines are embedded inside the decompiled
  C# source that the user views in a code editor; localizing them would make
  the resulting source mixed-language and harder to scan.

  [SettingsEntry(default, "description")] descriptions on IlSpySettings members
  intentionally stay in English in the source: the second arg of [SettingsEntry]
  must be a compile-time const, which excludes resource-manager lookups. To
  localize those, ReSharper's settings rendering pipeline would need a custom
  resolver — out of scope for the English-baseline infra pass. The
  IlSpySettings_* keys below are provided so a future custom resolver can
  pick them up without re-keying.
-->
